Fix Cocoa editor embedding and RGB buffer reads.

Keep the plugin view in the parent supplied by the host and return that
view as the LV2 widget. Do not resize the host window for an embedded UI,
and detach the editor view when it is destroyed.

Render using the actual RGB buffer dimensions and read exactly three bytes
per pixel. The old four-byte load overran the final pixel; using the host
view dimensions could also read beyond the backing buffer during resize.
Handle empty buffers and failed bitmap creation, and release image objects.

